From 9f46ef1f8e9a991bf9368ceeb6a9db2cf64eee96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Purtell <apurtell@apache.org>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:33:28 -0800
Subject: PHOENIX-5215 Addendum: OpenTelemetry packaging changes for 5.4

Backport of apache/phoenix commit 43cb24fe70, pushed to master as a
follow-up to PR #2586.

Adapted for 5.3.x: the ScanUtil.annotateMutationWithLiteralTTL call in
MutationState.sendMutations does not exist on this branch and is
omitted.

Packaging:
- The client jars no longer bundle the OpenTelemetry API. A bundled,
  unrelocated copy split the io.opentelemetry packages with the
  application's own copy. The jars now declare the API as a dependency,
  as hbase-shaded-client does. The assembly ships the API jars in lib,
  and the bin scripts add them to the classpath.
- phoenix-mapreduce-byo-shaded-hbase does not relocate io.opentelemetry.
- The OpenTelemetry BOM moves from the root dependencyManagement to the
  modules that compile against the API. Phoenix still compiles against
  1.15.0, but the packaged artifacts keep the version HBase declares.

MutationState:
- Restore the single catch (Exception) in sendMutations, so commit
  reports every failed batch as a CommitException again. Suppress
  SpotBugs REC_CATCH_EXCEPTION for that method.
- End the per-table span in one finally block, so it ends on every
  exit path, including failures before the batch is sent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
